  "guidance": "Combine data from multiple sources, stacked vertically, equivalent to a union in SQL.\n\nWhere headers differ, columns will be matched by name.\n\n```yaml\nread:\n  - union:\n      sources:\n        - file:\n            name: file1.xlsx\n        - file:\n            name: file2.xlsx\n```\n\n<div className=\"table-scroll\">\n<table>\n<tr><th></th><th></th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr>\n<tr><td>\n\n| column |\n| :-----: |\n| a |\n\n</td><td>\n\n\\+\n\n</td><td>\n\n| column |\n| :-----: |\n| b |\n\n</td><td>\n\n→\n</td><td>\n\n| column |\n| :-----: |\n| a |\n| b |\n\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n</div>\n\n> Union is the default aggregation for multiple reads."
